# vdbvisualizevelocity

- Label: VDB Visualize Velocity
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 1 to 1
- Parameters: 10 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/vdbvisualizevelocity.html
- Summary (EN): Traces streamers through a velocity VDB to show its flow. Outputs polylines and points representing the paths as geometry.
- Résumé (FR) : Trace des lignes de courant dans un VDB de vélocité et les sort en polylignes et points colorés selon la vitesse.

- Inputs meaning: ["v: a Vector VDB of velocities through which the streamers are traced"]

- Key parameters: ["Trail per Voxel: uses every voxel in the slicing plane as a streamer source", "Number Trails: scatters a fixed number of streamer sources, keeping density consistent across resolutions", "Plane: axis to extract, in the volume's local space", "Relative Location: slicing plane relative to the volume or in world coordinates", "Position: centre point where slicing starts in world coordinate mode", "Offset: positions the plane; relative mode range -1 to 1, 0 at the centre", "Trail Length: how long each trail lasts, in seconds", "Maximum Velocity: divides point speeds by this value to colour trails by speed"]

- Caveats: ["Trail per Voxel can get heavy with high resolutions", "In world coordinate mode the offset follows the world axis perpendicular to the plane, so it does not align with a rotated volume's axes"]

